WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.000
<b>Here Krishna wants to tell Arjuna:</b>

2
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.375
<b>You are in a forest of confusion</b>
<b>and attachment, Arjuna.</b>

3
00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:39.458
<b>When you emerge from this forest,</b>

4
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:47.666
<b>you may feel that everything you had heard </b>
<b>and known before was meaningless,</b>

5
00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:52.583
<b>and you will become detached from </b>
<b>those old learned concepts.</b>

6
00:00:57.375 --> 00:01:00.333
<b>Arjuna's mind was filled with many doubts.</b>

7
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:02.166
<b>Fear of family extinction,</b>

8
00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:04.833
<b>thoughts of being denied heaven,</b>

9
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:07.583
<b>the sin of killing his relatives.</b>

10
00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:12.916
<b>And Arjuna was citing knowledge from </b>
<b>the Vedas to support these concerns.</b>

11
00:01:12.916 --> 00:01:17.916
<b>The Vedas are often compared to a</b>
<b>wish-fulfilling tree (Kalpa-Vriksha). </b>

12
00:01:17.916 --> 00:01:22.833
<b>A tree so abundant that it </b>
<b>yields whatever fruit you seek.</b>

13
00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:29.541
<b>This tree is vast as a forest, and in this forest, </b>
<b>people often lose their way.</b>

14
00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:32.500
<b>If they set out seeking material fruits,</b>

15
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.541
<b>they find methods for that;</b>

16
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:38.500
<b>if they want spiritual fruits,</b>
<b>that path appears too.</b>

17
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.708
<b>Everything exists here, and this very </b>
<b>abundance confuses people.</b>

18
00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.291
<b>If fear already dwells in their mind,</b>

19
00:01:45.291 --> 00:01:51.333
<b>they will only see those elements </b>
<b>that strengthen this fear.</b>

20
00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:52.375
<b>Therefore,</b>

21
00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:58.625
<b>it's incorrect to view the Vedas through </b>
<b>the lens of pre-existing, fixed notions.</b>

22
00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:01.208
<b>Consider it this way:</b>

23
00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:02.875
<b>The great knowledge of the Vedas</b>

24
00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:06.125
<b>is like entering a university.</b>

25
00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:11.708
<b>Each person enters different </b>
<b>classes according to their level.</b>

26
00:02:11.708 --> 00:02:12.833
<b>Naturally,</b>

27
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:17.583
<b>the level of knowledge </b>
<b>varies with the class level.</b>

28
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:18.416
<b>But</b>

29
00:02:18.416 --> 00:02:24.541
<b>if someone remains stuck in one class, </b>
<b>believing it to be complete knowledge,</b>

30
00:02:24.541 --> 00:02:26.458
<b>would that be right?</b>

31
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:27.583
<b>No.</b>

32
00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:33.416
<b>For complete knowledge, you must graduate </b>
<b>from one class and move to higher classes.</b>

33
00:02:33.416 --> 00:02:38.625
<b>Only then will you graduate from this </b>
<b>university with higher education.</b>

34
00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.000
<b>To understand this further,</b>

35
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.125
<b>suppose</b>

36
00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:46.541
<b>in one class you're taught the means </b>
<b>to material pleasures.</b>

37
00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:50.291
<b>If, driven by material desires, </b>
<b>a person remains in that class</b>

38
00:02:50.291 --> 00:02:55.041
<b>and assumes the supreme purpose of the </b>
<b>Vedas is attaining material desires,</b>

39
00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.666
<b>wouldn't that be completely wrong?</b>

40
00:02:57.666 --> 00:02:58.375
<b>But</b>

41
00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:03.541
<b>one who has graduated from </b>
<b>all classes won't fall into this illusion.</b>

42
00:03:03.541 --> 00:03:06.250
<b>This is what Krishna wants to tell Arjuna...</b>

43
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:12.916
<b>that the Vedic knowledge you </b>
<b>cite to fear sin is correct,</b>

44
00:03:12.916 --> 00:03:13.625
<b>but</b>

45
00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:16.291
<b>it's not the highest level of Vedic knowledge.</b>

46
00:03:16.291 --> 00:03:20.750
<b>The supreme purpose of Vedic knowledge</b>
<b>is self-realization.</b>

47
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.375
<b>A level of knowledge that reveals</b>
<b>your spiritual truth,</b>

48
00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:28.458
<b>that unites the soul with the Divine.</b>

49
00:03:28.458 --> 00:03:30.875
<b>And when you reach that level,</b>

50
00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:35.958
<b>all previously heard concepts</b>
<b>will become meaningless.</b>

51
00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:42.333
<b>Arjuna's mind is</b>

52
00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:43.791
<b>filled with many thoughts,</b>

53
00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:45.416
<b>worries,</b>

54
00:03:45.416 --> 00:03:47.708
<b>and fears.</b>

55
00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:51.125
<b>That's why even in Vedic knowledge,</b>

56
00:03:51.125 --> 00:03:57.708
<b>he only sees what his fear wants him to see.</b>

57
00:03:57.708 --> 00:04:01.291
<b>This is making him more confused.</b>

58
00:04:01.291 --> 00:04:05.500
<b>Humans often wrestle with such situations.</b>

59
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.666
<b>You too must have experienced times</b>

60
00:04:07.666 --> 00:04:09.833
<b>when your mind was so full of thoughts</b>

61
00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:14.791
<b>and options that you became </b>
<b>completely perplexed.</b>

62
00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:20.041
<b>Unable to decide the right path.</b>

63
00:04:20.041 --> 00:04:25.041
<b>Others' suggestions only</b>
<b>complicate matters further.</b>

64
00:04:25.041 --> 00:04:27.916
<b>You were already burdened </b>
<b>with your own thoughts,</b>

65
00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:33.375
<b>now you carry the weight of others' opinions too.</b>

66
00:04:33.375 --> 00:04:36.208
<b>Nothing makes sense.</b>

67
00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.041
<b>Peace.</b>

68
00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:41.875
<b>First and foremost, peace.</b>

69
00:04:41.875 --> 00:04:48.125
<b>Take a deep breath.</b>

70
00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:53.500
<b>Now calmly observe your situation.</b>

71
00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.333
<b>Ask yourself:</b>

72
00:04:56.333 --> 00:05:00.750
<b>What is your life's purpose?</b>

73
00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.541
<b>For example,</b>

74
00:05:02.541 --> 00:05:09.250
<b>you're unsure whether to say yes or no to a task.</b>

75
00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:15.041
<b>Your life's purpose is to contribute </b>
<b>something to society.</b>

76
00:05:15.041 --> 00:05:23.000
<b>So, does this task bring you closer</b>
<b>to your life's purpose?</b>

77
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.541
<b>Then try to understand </b>
<b>what you want to become.</b>

78
00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:33.166
<b>Think beyond material desires here. </b>
<b>Find the answer.</b>

79
00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:39.375
<b>‘Not that I want to become wealthy, </b>
<b>I want to become a high official.’</b>

80
00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:44.000
<b>Rather, I want to become a good person,</b>

81
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.416
<b>an excellent teacher,</b>

82
00:05:47.416 --> 00:05:50.541
<b>a great athlete,</b>

83
00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:52.958
<b>and so on.</b>

84
00:05:52.958 --> 00:05:58.750
<b>Through this thought process, you'll gradually </b>
<b>emerge from the forest of confusion.</b>

85
00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:03.458
<b>And when this happens, the noise of </b>
<b>others' suggestions will fade, </b>

86
00:06:03.458 --> 00:06:07.750
<b>and the path will become clear.</b>

87
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.958
<b>Now,</b>

88
00:06:09.958 --> 00:06:12.500
<b>just start walking on that path.</b>

89
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.333
<b>If this situation arises again,</b>

90
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:18.541
<b>reflect once more.</b>

91
00:06:18.541 --> 00:06:21.166
<b>This is a continuous process.</b>

92
00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:23.333
<b>Know yourself,</b>

93
00:06:23.333 --> 00:06:28.041
<b>and gradually you'll know everything.</b>

94
00:06:32.833 --> 00:06:38.166
<b>When you're emerging from </b>
<b>an emotional struggle in life,</b>

95
00:06:38.166 --> 00:06:42.708
<b>everything appears hazy to the mind.</b>

96
00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:44.291
<b>What to do,</b>

97
00:06:44.291 --> 00:06:45.458
<b>what not to do.</b>

98
00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:48.625
<b>Nothing makes sense.</b>

99
00:06:48.625 --> 00:06:49.666
<b>In such times,</b>

100
00:06:49.666 --> 00:06:53.125
<b>everyone tries to offer their advice.</b>

101
00:06:53.125 --> 00:06:54.166
<b>Perhaps</b>

102
00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:57.250
<b>you too have attempted this.</b>

103
00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:03.083
<b>You may have tried to explain</b>
<b>to a friend caught in emotions</b>

104
00:07:03.083 --> 00:07:05.083
<b>that worry is futile.</b>

105
00:07:05.083 --> 00:07:07.750
<b>Though the intention may be good,</b>

106
00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:17.833
<b>from experience you know such suggestions </b>
<b>don't solve the problem.</b>

107
00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:19.166
<b>So</b>

108
00:07:19.166 --> 00:07:21.291
<b>what should be done?</b>

109
00:07:21.291 --> 00:07:25.333
<b>As long as the dust of emotions swirls,</b>

110
00:07:25.333 --> 00:07:27.583
<b>nothing will be clear.</b>

111
00:07:27.583 --> 00:07:34.375
<b>If you're in this situation, </b>
<b>or helping someone else,</b>

112
00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:36.041
<b>it's first </b>

113
00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:41.958
<b>essential to let the intensity of emotions subside.</b>

114
00:07:41.958 --> 00:07:43.000
<b>For this,</b>

115
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:50.041
<b>understand that perhaps the situation</b>
<b>isn't as dire as you think.</b>

116
00:07:50.041 --> 00:07:54.708
<b>This will bring some emotional stability.</b>

117
00:07:54.708 --> 00:07:56.416
<b>Then,</b>

118
00:07:56.416 --> 00:08:01.666
<b>calmly consider what options you have.</b>

119
00:08:01.666 --> 00:08:02.833
<b>Next,</b>

120
00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:06.958
<b>weigh the consequences of these options.</b>

121
00:08:06.958 --> 00:08:08.250
<b>In this process,</b>

122
00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:14.000
<b>we're moving from emotionality </b>
<b>toward logic and wisdom.</b>

123
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.583
<b>As this happens, everything will </b>
<b>gradually become clear.</b>

124
00:08:18.583 --> 00:08:22.916
<b>The path to choose will become evident.</b>

125
00:08:22.916 --> 00:08:23.875
<b>Therefore,</b>

126
00:08:23.875 --> 00:08:30.833
<b>whether helping yourself or </b>
<b>others, first stabilize emotions,</b>

127
00:08:30.833 --> 00:08:34.416
<b>then seek answers in </b>
<b>the light of logic and wisdom.</b>

128
00:08:39.166 --> 00:08:46.583
<b>If you're a senior official in an </b>
<b>organization or lead many people,</b>

129
00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:54.416
<b>a significant part of your responsibility</b>
<b>becomes how you make decisions,</b>

130
00:08:54.416 --> 00:08:57.791
<b>and even more importantly,</b>

131
00:08:57.791 --> 00:09:04.291
<b>how you contribute to improving your </b>
<b>colleagues' decision-making abilities.</b>

132
00:09:04.291 --> 00:09:05.541
<b>Because when</b>

133
00:09:05.541 --> 00:09:07.791
<b>colleagues make right decisions,</b>

134
00:09:07.791 --> 00:09:13.041
<b>it helps both you and the </b>
<b>organization's purpose.</b>

135
00:09:13.041 --> 00:09:16.500
<b>For this, two things need attention:</b>

136
00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:17.541
<b>First thing</b>

137
00:09:17.541 --> 00:09:20.583
<b>- People should remain emotionally stable.</b>

138
00:09:20.583 --> 00:09:27.208
<b>If feelings like mutual jealousy, </b>
<b>disagreements, fear arise,</b>

139
00:09:27.208 --> 00:09:30.291
<b>they will diminish decision-making ability.</b>

140
00:09:30.291 --> 00:09:31.291
<b>Therefore,</b>

141
00:09:31.291 --> 00:09:36.375
<b>create an environment free </b>
<b>from fear and jealousy.</b>

142
00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:41.416
<b>Treating everyone equally will help in this.</b>

143
00:09:41.416 --> 00:09:42.958
<b>And second</b>

144
00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:47.208
<b>- Connect people's objectives</b>
<b>with the organization's goals.</b>

145
00:09:47.208 --> 00:09:56.625
<b>Bring clarity about how achieving organizational </b>
<b>goals will fulfill their personal objectives.</b>

146
00:09:56.625 --> 00:10:03.208
<b>By doing this, they'll rise above self-interest </b>
<b>and adopt a broader perspective.</b>

147
00:10:03.208 --> 00:10:05.166
<b>Remember:</b>

148
00:10:05.166 --> 00:10:08.541
<b>If a group is free from mutual jealousy</b>

149
00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:12.333
<b>and everyone is connected to one purpose,</b>

150
00:10:12.333 --> 00:10:15.791
<b>their decisions will be in the right direction.</b>

151
00:10:15.791 --> 00:10:19.583
<b>You only need to support them.</b>

152
00:10:19.583 --> 00:10:23.041
<b>This will lead to everyone's professional growth.</b>

